- Vmag (apparent magnitude): Generally, apparent magnitude alone is not a direct indicator of giant status because it depends on distance. However, very bright apparent stars might be giants if distant.
- Plx (parallax): Smaller parallax means greater distance; giants are often more luminous and can be seen at larger distances with moderate brightness.
- e_Plx (error in parallax): High errors reduce reliability of distance and absolute magnitude calculations.
