- Vmag (apparent visual magnitude): Brighter stars (lower Vmag) tend to be closer or intrinsically brighter; however, apparent brightness alone is not a strong indicator of giant status due to distance effects.  
- Plx (parallax): Larger parallax means closer star; smaller parallax means farther star. Giants can be farther but still bright intrinsically, so smaller parallax may indicate giants if apparent magnitude is moderate.  
